{
 "id": "ship-of-theseus",
 "channel": "philosophy",
 "style": "clay",
 "title": "THE SHIP OF THESEUS",
 "angle": "If every part of something is replaced, is it still the same thing, and what does that make you?",
 "hooks": [
  "Is a ship with every plank replaced still the same ship?",
  "Most of your body is younger than you are."
 ],
 "world": {
  "scenery": "open",
  "ground": "#F3DEC0"
 },
 "script": [
  {
   "text": "Every twenty years, Japan tears down its holiest shrine and rebuilds it.",
   "beat": "hook"
  },
  {
   "text": "Yet the shrine is said to be thirteen centuries old.",
   "beat": "hook",
   "link": "but"
  },
  {
   "text": "So if every part is replaced, is it still the same thing?",
   "beat": "question",
   "link": "so"
  },
  {
   "text": "The answer, it turns out, is about you.",
   "beat": "question",
   "link": "detail"
  },
  {
   "text": "Ancient Athens tried it for real, with the ship of the hero Theseus.",
   "beat": "reveal1",
   "link": "answer"
  },
  {
   "text": "For centuries, as each plank rotted, they swapped in a new one.",
   "beat": "reveal1",
   "link": "detail"
  },
  {
   "text": "So philosophers argued: was it still his ship?",
   "beat": "reveal1",
   "link": "so"
  },
  {
   "text": "But in 1655, Thomas Hobbes made it much worse.",
   "beat": "reveal2",
   "link": "but",
   "say": "But in sixteen fifty-five, Thomas Hobbes made it much worse."
  },
  {
   "text": "Suppose someone kept every old plank and rebuilt the original ship beside it.",
   "beat": "reveal2",
   "link": "detail"
  },
  {
   "text": "Now there are two ships, and only one can be Theseus's.",
   "beat": "reveal2",
   "link": "so"
  },
  {
   "text": "So researchers asked about three thousand people in twenty-two countries.",
   "beat": "reveal3",
   "link": "so"
  },
  {
   "text": "Again and again, one question tipped the answer: does it still do its job?",
   "beat": "reveal3",
   "link": "detail"
  },
  {
   "text": "Ise agrees: the new shrine does the job, and its old pillars become gates at other shrines.",
   "beat": "reveal3",
   "link": "detail",
   "say": "Ee-seh agrees: the new shrine does the job, and its old pillars become gates at other shrines."
  },
  {
   "text": "But you are a ship of Theseus too.",
   "beat": "turn",
   "link": "but"
  },
  {
   "text": "Scientists dated your cells with carbon from Cold War bomb tests, and most are younger than you.",
   "beat": "turn",
   "link": "detail"
  },
  {
   "text": "But the neurons of your cortex seem to be as old as you.",
   "beat": "payoff",
   "link": "but"
  },
  {
   "text": "So what keeps you you: the parts that stayed, or the job they keep doing?",
   "beat": "payoff",
   "link": "so"
  }
 ],
